-- Points every book's cover_url at our own newly-populated Storage
-- bucket (book-covers, created in 20260918200000) instead of
-- Hardcover's live CDN. All 1254 images were downloaded from each
-- book's existing cover_url and uploaded via `supabase storage cp -r`
-- (see docs/project-log.md's 2026-09-18 entry for the full pipeline).
-- Filename per object is the book's own id, so this UPDATE can be
-- generated directly from that id -- no title-matching needed, unlike
-- every other title-scoped migration in this project. Generated
-- directly from the REAL bucket listing (not local download metadata)
-- so the extension always matches what's actually stored -- one file
-- (a single manually-retried download after a transient DNS failure
-- during the bulk download) kept its original .jpeg extension instead
-- of the .jpg the rest of the batch normalized to, and generating
-- from local metadata instead of the real listing would have missed
-- that and produced a 404ing URL for that one book.

